\paragraph{Practical magnitude.}
\label{sec:practical_magnitude}
\looseness=-1
Direct regression on 100 random 16-type batches within the 80-relation pool yields a conservative restricted-range estimate ($r = -0.22$, $R^2 \approx 0.05$, $p = 0.027$) due to narrow BCS range (SD${}\,=\,0.044$ vs.\ pooled SD${}\,=\,0.141$). The pooled analysis (semipartial $R^2 = 0.273$, $n = 204$; \S\ref{sec:bcs_controlled}) provides the primary variance estimate; DocRED pooled $R^2 = 0.578$ ($n = 110$) is inflated by multicollinearity (VIF${}\,=\,50.9$; semipartial $R^2_{\text{BCS}} = 0.056$; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_partial_corr}). The amplification from pairwise $r^2 \approx 1.5\%$ to pooled semipartial $R^2 \approx 27.3\%$ reflects the operative mechanism: correlated confusable-type interactions compound within shared prompts \citep{robinson-1950-ecological,baan-2023-ecological}, producing the batch-level signal (${\sim}3\times$ amplification; Monte Carlo simulation in Appendix~\ref{app:aggregation-sim}).

